  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Develop a national Climate Atlas projecting climate change at re-gional level in Ghana for different global greenhouse gas emission scenarios</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="280358" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">GMET is able to operate and maintain National Climate Atlas</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2025-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="A functional prototype that can operate at GMET is developed."></target>
     <actual value="DMI has assisted the partners in developing the scientific foundation for Climate Atlas for Ghana  for three key climate parameters: temperature, precipitation and sea level rise. Development of front end is ongoing with planned finalization in 2025. The Climate Atlas for Ghana delivers a unified platform and repository of data, that provides the foundation for a science based approach to climate action in Ghana.

Ghana Metrological institutes capacity to train and educate meteorologists and forecasters in compliance with international (WMO and ICAO) standards is improving. Development of course structure is training syllabus making progress. By supporting GMET to comply with international standards, the project supports GMET in obtaining a sustainable source of income. With a steady flow of funds, GMET can prioritize resources towards building their general forecasting capacity and strengthen forecasts for early warning throughout Ghana."></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Three key climate parameters, temperature, precipitation and sea level rise developed"></target>
     <actual value="Three key climate parameters, temperature, precipitation and sea level rise developed"></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2026-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2026-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="A full functional Climate Atlas Ghana that can operate at GMET."></target>
     <actual></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
